{
  "schema": "audience-origin-rules.v1",
  "purpose": "Reviewed bilingual rules of the standing audience-origin check (decision 0035 items 1 and 5; document 15, Standing audience-origin check). Terms are matched on whole words after normalisation (NFC, Arabic diacritics and tatweel removed, alef variants folded, case folded). A 'violation' term is an origin label wherever it is not excused; a 'review' term reports an unclassified candidate use that also fails, until a reviewed allowance covers it. allow_contexts are reviewed phrases that excuse a term inside them; allow_values are reviewed whole strings that excuse any term inside them. Arabic rules reuse the approved lexicon of S3-T18 and are marked pending native review.",
